comments.body:
*Released product: likely not affected.* Confidence: high. Grounding: unaffected-version. Released mongodb\-mcp\-server@3.2.2 resolves proxy\-addr 2.0.8, not the ticket's 2.0.7. The advisory affects >= 1.1.0 < 2.0.8, and 2.0.8 is the first patched version whose shipped code contains the fix. Production reaches proxy\-addr only through express 5.3.0, which itself requires proxy\-addr \^2.0.8, so an affected 2.0.7 build cannot be installed from the released manifests. Likely not affected.

Assessed targets: current main commit 6143ab66116f73ccccd94ab207ce85db6bdb0d50; released product mongodb\-mcp\-server@3.2.2 (commit 0af7e43bd2c8d0188644b355bbc25da8c7c62d98). Ticket created 2026\-10\-06. Recommendation only; final decision remains with the reviewer.
{anchor:mongodb-vulnerability-auto-triage-v1-release-989a98f0a655094067e51b85c9697e6258bce582bd325a4c0753fda226b2193f}

*Current main: likely not affected.* Confidence: high. Grounding: unaffected-version. Current main (6143ab66) resolves proxy\-addr 2.0.8 on every production and dev path in a complete pnpm lockfile graph; 2.0.7 appears nowhere. The advisory affects >= 1.1.0 < 2.0.8, and 2.0.8 is the first patched version whose shipped code contains the mapped\-IPv6 trust\-subnet guard. The ticket's 2.0.7 refers to an older build that does not match this target. Likely not affected.

